  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Pb</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ag</mi></math> commonly exist in the form of sulphide ore like <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PbS</mi></math> (galena) and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Ag</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> (Argentite) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Al</mi></math>&nbsp;is mainly found in the form of oxide ore whereas &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mg</mi></math> is found in the form of halide ore."
